"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CQ1.1</strong> — What is C programming language, and what are its primary uses?</li>\n<li><strong>CQ1.2</strong> — What are the basic structure and syntax of a C program?</li>\n<li><strong>CQ1.3</strong> — What does the #include preprocessor directive do?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — Slot 00 Course Introduction (21 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">⚠️ ESTIMATED placement — the deck name gives no session/chapter number. File: Slot_00_Course Introduction.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — Slot 00 Course Introduction (21 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">⚠️ GHÉP ƯỚC LƯỢNG — tên deck không ghi số buổi/chương, cần soát lại. Tệp: Slot_00_Course Introduction.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/001.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 1: C++ Programming\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 1/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>C++ Programming</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/002.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 2: Contents\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 2/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Contents<br>Why should you study this course?<br>Prerequisites<br>Course Objectives<br>Course Description and Course Plan<br>Materials/ References/ Tools<br>Course Rules<br>Evaluation Strategy<br>How to study<br>Academic policy<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/003.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 3: Why should you study this course?\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 3/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Why should you study this course?<br>‹#›<br>Performance &amp; Efficiency: C++ is a high-performance language that allows direct memory manipulation, making it ideal for system-level programming, game development, and applications requiring speed and efficiency.<br>Foundation for Other Languages: Understanding C++ makes it easier to learn other programming languages like Java, and C#. Many modern languages derive concepts from C++.<br>Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): C++ supports OOP principles such as encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism, helping you develop scalable and maintainable software.<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/004.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 4: Why should you study this course?\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 4/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Why should you study this course?<br>‹#›<br>Widely Used in Industry: C++ is used in various fields, including game development, system programming (operating systems, drivers), embedded systems, and financial applications.<br>Competitive Programming &amp; Problem Solving: C++ is the preferred language for competitive programming due to its fast execution speed and rich Standard Template Library (STL) for handling complex algorithms efficiently.<br>Cross-Platform Development: C++ allows you to develop applications that can run on multiple platforms, including Windows, Linux, and macOS, with minimal modifications.<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/005.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 5: Why C++ is chosen?\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 5/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Why C++ is chosen?<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025<br>Applications of C++</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/006.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 6: Completed:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 6/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Completed:<br>PRF192<br>‹#›<br>Prerequisites<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/007.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 7: Course Objectives\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 7/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Objectives<br>Understand the Fundamentals of C++<br>Master C++ syntax, data types, operators, and control structures.<br>Apply Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) Concepts<br>Learn and implement OOP principles such as inheritance, encapsulation, polymorphism, and abstraction.<br>Enhance Problem-Solving Skills<br>Use C++ to solve algorithmic problems, optimize code, and participate in competitive programming.<br>Develop Efficient and Scalable Programs<br>Manage memory efficiently, optimize performance, and handle errors effectively in C++.<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/008.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 8: Course Objectives (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 8/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Objectives (cont.)<br>Work with Data Structures and Algorithms<br>Utilize the Standard Template Library (STL) and implement common data structures like linked lists, queues, stacks, and trees.<br>Understand File Handling<br>Learn how to read/write files<br>Explore Advanced Topics in C++<br>Work with multithreading, smart pointers, and system-level programming.<br>Develop Real-World Applications<br>Build practical projects such as management software, simple games, or high-performance computing applications.<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/009.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 9: Course Description\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 9/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Description<br>Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax<br>Get familiar with C++ syntax, structure, and the compilation process.<br>Operators, Expressions, and Basic I/O<br>Work with operators, expressions, and implement basic input/output operations.<br>Control Structures - Decision Making and Loops<br>Learn to use decision-making statements and loops for program flow control.<br>Arrays and Pointer Fundamentals<br>Gain a strong understanding of arrays and their interaction with pointers.<br>Dynamic Memory Allocation &amp; Advanced Pointer Usage<br>Learn dynamic memory management and avoid common pointer-related pitfalls.<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/010.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 10: Course Description (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 10/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Description (cont.)<br>Structs, Unions, and Complex Data Organization<br>Organize and manage complex data using structs, unions<br>Memory Management and Performance Optimization<br>Optimize memory usage, prevent leaks, and enhance performance with smart pointers.<br>Functions, Overloading, and Template Programming<br>Learn to write modular and reusable C++ code using functions, function overloading, and templates.<br>Scope, Namespaces, and Visibility Rules<br>Manage variable scope, apply namespaces for modularity, and ensure maintainable code structure.<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/011.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 11: Course Description (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 11/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Description (cont.)<br>Introduction to STL Containers &amp; Algorithms<br>Learn the fundamentals of STL containers and algorithms for efficient programming.<br>Introduction to STL Features &amp; Optimization<br>Explore basic STL features, optimize performance, and practice real-world STL applications.<br>Introduction to Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) &amp; Encapsulation<br>Understand the fundamentals of OOP and implement encapsulation for modular programming.<br>Inheritance – Code Reusability &amp; Hierarchical Design<br>Learn how inheritance promotes code reusability and implement hierarchical class structures.<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/012.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 12: Course Description (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 12/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Description (cont.)<br>Polymorphism &amp; Special Member Functions<br>Master polymorphism and learn to manage object lifecycles using special member functions.<br>Exception Handling &amp; Robust Application Design<br>Build error-resistant programs using exception handling mechanisms.<br>Text and Binary File Handling &amp; File Processing<br>Learn to work with text and binary files, and manipulate file data.<br>Preprocessor Directives &amp; Type Conversions<br>Master preprocessor directives for code optimization and understand type conversions for safer data manipulation.<br>Smart Pointers, Multithreading, and Lambda Expressions<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/013.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 13: Course Plan\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 13/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Plan<br>See course plan on FLM<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/014.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 14: Materials/ References\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 14/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Materials/ References<br>MOOC: Introduction to Object Oriented Programming (C++)<br>Author: Chris Szalwinski and Seneca College<br>Online: https://intro2oop.sdds.ca/<br>2) Beginning C++ Programming - Reference<br>Author: Richard Grimes<br>Published Date: April 24, 2017; Edition: 2nd Edtitions<br>3) C++ Primer - Reference<br>Authors: Stanley B. Lippman, José Lajoie, Barbara E. Moo<br>Published Date: 2012; 5th Edition<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/015.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 15: Tools\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 15/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Tools<br>Tool (IDE): Dev-C++ version 6.3  (TDM-GCC 9.2.0)<br>Link download: https://sourceforge.net/projects/embarcadero-devcpp/<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/016.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 16: Course Rules\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 16/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Rules<br>How to conduct<br>Prepare contents of the next session at home<br>Following lessons in classroom<br>Completing chapter assessments in time and Quizzes (https://exam.fpt.edu.vn)<br>Write reports of all labs and assignments to your notebook<br>Communication<br>Class<br>Interchange by CMS, EduNext<br>Discussing actively in your team and classroom<br>Free to question and answer<br>Others<br>Off phone, no game, no chat in class<br>Use laptop under teacher’s instruction<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/017.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 17: Evaluation Strategy\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 17/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Evaluation Strategy<br>Must attend at least 80% of contact hours (if not, not allow to take exam)<br>Evaluating<br>Maximum score: 10<br>On-going assessments:<br>02 Progress Test (PT, 15%)<br>05 Workshops (WS, 10%)<br>01 Assignment (AS, 15%)<br>01 Practical Exam (PE, 30%)<br>Final Exam (FE, 30%)<br>Final Result = 0.15*PT + 0.1*WS + 0.15*AS + 0.3*PE + 0.3*FE<br>Pass:<br>Every on-going assessments component &gt;0<br>Practical Exam (PE) &gt;= 2; Final Exam (FE) Score &gt;= 4 and  Final Result  &gt;= 5<br>Final Exam retake only when not passed<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/018.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 18: How to study\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 18/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>How to study<br>This course is complex knowledge (however, it’s attractive and exciting), so you need to keep a tight grip on it<br>Read<br>On the books to get the general concept<br>Reference, study, collection from anywhere else (internet, your classmate, forum …)<br>Attend lectures<br>Listen, understand, then make your notes<br>Give your explanation about some topic in lectures<br>Ask questions<br>Give some examples that do not exist in your book<br>Practice all the exercises, demo to make your sense<br>After classes<br>Discuss your classmate indirectly, on the forum<br>Analyze, design, and implement workshops and assignments. Write reports in your notebook<br>Build your team in yourselves to support together in studying<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/019.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 19: Academic policy\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 19/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Academic policy<br>Cheating, plagiarism and breach of copyright are serious offenses under this Policy.<br>Cheating<br>Cheating during a test or exam is construed as talking, peeking at another student’s paper or any other clandestine method of transmitting information.<br>Plagiarism<br>Plagiarism is using the work of others without citing it; that is, holding the work of others out as your own work.<br>Breach of Copyright<br>If you photocopy a textbook without the copyright holder's permission, you violate copyright law.<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/020.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 20: Enjoy the Course\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 20/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Enjoy the Course<br>Be enthusiastic about the material because it is interesting, useful and an important part of your training as a software engineer.<br>Our job is to help you learn and enjoy the experience.<br>We will do our best but we need your help.<br>So let’s all have fun together with C++ Programming !!!<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d01/021.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 21: Q &amp; A\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 00 Course Introduction · slide 21/21</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Q &amp; A<br>‹#›<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>🔗 Links on these slides — watch/read them</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>🔗 Link trong slide — xem/đọc thêm</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://intro2oop.sdds.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://intro2oop.sdds.ca/</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/embarcadero-devcpp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://sourceforge.net/projects/embarcadero-devcpp/</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://exam.fpt.edu.vn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://exam.fpt.edu.vn</a></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax (43 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by the session number in the deck name. File: Slot_01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax (43 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo số buổi ghi trong tên deck. Tệp: Slot_01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/001.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 1: Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 1/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/002.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 2: Objectives\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 2/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Objectives<br>Understand the basic structure of a C++ program.<br>Learn how C++ code is compiled and executed.<br>Familiarize with data types, variables, and constants in C++.<br>2<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/003.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 3: Contents\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 3/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Contents<br>Introduction to C++ and Development Environment<br>Program Structure and Compilation Process<br>Data Types, Variables, and Constants<br>Hands-on exercises<br>3<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/004.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 4: Introduction to C++ and Development Environment\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 4/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Introduction to C++ and Development Environment</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/005.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 5: History of C++\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 5/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>History of C++<br>C++ was developed by Bjarne Stroustrup at Bell Labs in 1979 as an extension of the C language. Initially called &quot;C with Classes,&quot; it introduced object-oriented programming (OOP) to improve C’s capabilities. In 1983, the language was renamed C++, where &quot;++&quot; represents the increment operator in C, symbolizing its evolution.<br>5<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/006.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 6: Key milestones in C++ history (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 6/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Key milestones in C++ history (cont.)<br>1985 - First official release of C++.<br>1990 - Introduction of The Annotated C++ Reference Manual, leading to the standardization of the language.<br>1998 - First C++ standard (C++98), introducing the Standard Template Library (STL).<br>2011 (C++11) – Major updates, including smart pointers, lambda expressions, and multithreading support.<br>2014, 2017, 2020 – Further enhancements for performance, safety, and modern programming paradigms.<br>6<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/007.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 7: Key Features of C++\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 7/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Key Features of C++<br>Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)<br>Supports classes, objects, inheritance, polymorphism, encapsulation, and abstraction.<br>High Performance<br>Provides direct memory manipulation and is faster than many high-level languages.<br>Multi-Paradigm Language<br>Supports procedural, object-oriented, and generic programming.<br>Memory Management<br>Allows manual memory control with pointers, dynamic allocation (new/delete), and smart pointers (unique_ptr, shared_ptr).<br>7<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/008.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 8: Key Features of C++ (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 8/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Key Features of C++ (cont.)<br>Standard Template Library (STL)<br>Includes pre-built containers, algorithms, and iterators for efficient programming.<br>Portability &amp; Cross-Platform Compatibility<br>Code can be compiled and run on multiple operating systems with minimal modifications.<br>Extensibility &amp; Scalability<br>Suitable for small programs to large-scale applications like game engines, real-time simulations, and financial systems.<br>8<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/009.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 9: Key Features of C++ (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 9/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Key Features of C++ (cont.)<br>Low-Level and High-Level Programming<br>Combines high-level abstraction with low-level hardware access, making it ideal for embedded systems and operating systems.<br>Concurrency &amp; Multithreading<br>Supports thread management for high-performance applications.<br>Backward Compatibility with C<br>C++ can run most C programs, making it easy for C programmers to transition.<br>9<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/010.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 10: Applications of C++\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 10/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Applications of C++<br>10<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/011.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 11: Writing Your First C++ Program in Windows\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 11/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Writing Your First C++ Program in Windows<br>Create a new C++ file<br>Open Dev-C++ (version 6.3) → Click File → New → Source File<br>Typing the following code:<br>Save the file as hello.cpp<br>11<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/012.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 12: Writing Your First C++ Program in Windows\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 12/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Writing Your First C++ Program in Windows<br>Compile and Run the Program<br>Step 1: Press F9 to compile the code.<br>Step 2: Press F10 to run the program.<br>Step 3: The output will be displayed in the Command Prompt (CMD):<br>12<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/013.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 13: Program Structure and Compilation Process\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 13/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Program Structure and Compilation Process</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/014.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 14: Overview of C++ Program Structure\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 14/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Overview of C++ Program Structure<br>A simple C++ program consists of the following:<br>14<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/015.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 15: Key Components\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 15/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Key Components<br>Component<br>Description<br>#include &lt;iostream&gt;<br>Preprocessor directive to include the I/O library<br>using namespace std;<br>Allows use of standard functions without std:: prefix<br>int main()<br>The main function, entry point of the program<br>{ ... }<br>Code block containing program instructions<br>cout &lt;&lt; ...;<br>Outputs text to the console<br>return 0;<br>Ends the program and returns 0 to the OS<br>15<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/016.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 16: Comments in C++\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 16/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Comments in C++<br>Comments help in making code readable.<br>Single-line comment: // This is a comment<br>Multi-line comment:<br>16<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/017.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 17: Compilation Process in C++\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 17/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Compilation Process in C++<br>17<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/018.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 18: Compilation Process in C++ (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 18/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Compilation Process in C++ (cont.)<br>C++ is a compiled language, meaning the source code must be converted to machine code before execution.<br>Compilation Steps:<br>Step 1. Preprocessing → Expands #include, #define, removes comments.<br>Step 2. Compiling → Translates .cpp source code into assembly code (.s)<br>Step 3. Assembling → Converts assembly code into machine code (.o)<br>Step 4. Linking → Combines object files into an executable (.exe)<br>18<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/019.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 19: Data Types, Variables, and Constants\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 19/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Data Types, Variables, and Constants</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/020.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 20: Data Types\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 20/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Data Types<br>In C++, data is categorized into primitive types and complex types. Below is a detailed breakdown of each category.<br>Primitive Data Types<br>Character &amp; String Data Types<br>Extended Integer Types<br>Extended Floating-Point Types<br>Data Type Modifiers<br>Pointer Data Types<br>20<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/021.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 21: 1. Primitive Data Types\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 21/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>1. Primitive Data Types<br>Primitive data types in C++ include integers, floating-point numbers, characters, and boolean values.<br>21<br>24/03/2025<br>Data Type<br>Description<br>Size (bytes)<br>Example Values<br>int<br>Integer numbers<br>4<br>10, -50, 1000<br>float<br>Single-precision floating-point<br>4<br>3.14, -0.001<br>double<br>Double-precision floating-point<br>8<br>3.1415926535<br>char<br>Single ASCII character<br>1<br>'A', 'z', '9'<br>bool<br>Boolean true/false value<br>1<br>true, false</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/022.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 22: 1. Primative Data Types (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 22/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>1. Primative Data Types (cont.)<br>Example: Using Basic Data Types<br>22<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/023.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 23: 2. Character &amp; String Data Types\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 23/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. Character &amp; String Data Types<br>C++ supports working with strings using character arrays (char[]) or the std::string class.<br>23<br>24/03/2025<br>Data Type<br>Description<br>Example<br>char<br>Single ASCII character<br>'A', '9'<br>char[]<br>C-style string (character array)<br>&quot;Hello&quot;<br>string<br>String from &lt;string&gt; library<br>&quot;C++ Programming&quot;</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/024.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 24: 2. Character &amp; String Data Types (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 24/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. Character &amp; String Data Types (cont.)<br>Example: Using char[] and string<br>Note: The string type in C++ provides built-in methods such as .length(), .append(), and .substr(), making it more versatile than char[].<br>24<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/025.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 25: 3. Extended Integer Types\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 25/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>3. Extended Integer Types<br>C++ provides various integer types to optimize memory usage and performance.<br>25<br>24/03/2025<br>Data Type<br>Size (bytes)<br>Value Range<br>short int (short)<br>2<br>-32,768 to 32,767<br>int<br>4<br>-2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647<br>long int (long)<br>4 or 8<br>-2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647 (on 32-bit systems)<br>long long int (long long)<br>8<br>-9,223,372,036,854,775,808 to 9,223,372,036,854,775,807</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/026.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 26: 3. Extended Integer Types (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 26/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>3. Extended Integer Types (cont.)<br>Example: Using Extended Integer Types<br>Note: On 64-bit systems, long can be 8 bytes, while on 32-bit systems, it remains 4 bytes.<br>26<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/027.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 27: 4. Extended Floating-Point Types\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 27/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>4. Extended Floating-Point Types<br>In addition to float and double, C++ provides long double for high-precision calculations.<br>Use sizeof(long double) to check the actual size on your system!<br>27<br>24/03/2025<br>Data Type<br>Size (bytes)<br>Precision<br>float<br>4<br>~7 decimal places<br>double<br>8<br>~15 decimal places<br>long double<br>10, 12, 16<br>~18+ decimal places</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/028.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 28: 4. Extended Floating-Point Types (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 28/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>4. Extended Floating-Point Types (cont.)<br>The size of long double depends on the compiler, architecture, and memory alignment:<br>10 bytes: On 32-bit (x86) systems using x87 FPU with GCC/Clang, stored in 80-bit extended precision format.<br>12 bytes: On some 32-bit systems, due to memory alignment, padding 2 extra bytes.<br>16 bytes: On 64-bit (x86-64) systems with GCC/Clang, using 128-bit storage for better precision.<br>Windows (MSVC): long double is usually 8 bytes (same as double).<br>Linux/macOS (GCC/Clang): Typically 10, 12, or 16 bytes, depending on architecture.<br>28<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/029.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 29: 4. Extended Floating-Point Types (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 29/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>4. Extended Floating-Point Types (cont.)<br>Example: Using Extended Floating-Point Types<br>29<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/030.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 30: 5. Data Type Modifiers\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 30/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5. Data Type Modifiers<br>C++ provides modifiers to adjust the storage and value range of data types.<br>30<br>24/03/2025<br>Modifier<br>Meaning<br>signed<br>Allows both positive and negative values (default)<br>unsigned<br>Only allows positive values<br>short<br>Reduces size of int<br>long<br>Increases size of int or double</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/031.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 31: 5. Data Type Modifiers (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 31/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5. Data Type Modifiers (cont.)<br>Example: Using unsigned and signed<br>Note: Use unsigned when you know the variable will only store positive values.<br>31<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/032.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 32: C++ supports pointers, which store the memory address of a variable.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 32/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>C++ supports pointers, which store the memory address of a variable.<br>Example: Basic Pointer Usage<br>Note: Pointers are crucial for working with arrays, dynamic memory allocation, and efficient memory management.<br>6. Pointer Data Types<br>32<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/033.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 33: Variables\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 33/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables<br>In C++, a variable is a named storage location in memory that holds a value. Each variable has a type, which determines the size and layout of its memory, the range of values it can store, and the operations that can be performed on it.<br>For example:<br>33<br>24/03/2025<br>Syntax: data_type identifier [= initial value];</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/034.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 34: Variables (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 34/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables (cont.)<br>Rules for naming variables are:<br>Names can contain letters, digits and underscores.<br>Names must begin with a letter or an underscore (_)<br>Names are case-sensitive (myVar and myvar are different variables)<br>Names cannot contain whitespaces or special characters like !, #, %, etc.<br>Avoid C++ reserved keywords:<br>34<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/035.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 35: Variables (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 35/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables (cont.)<br>Declaration of variables:<br>C++ is a strongly-typed language, and requires every variable to be declared with its type before its first use.<br>This informs the compiler the size to reserve in memory for the variable and how to interpret its value.<br>35<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/036.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 36: Variables (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 36/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables (cont.)<br>Initialization of variables:<br>Variables can have a specific value from the moment they are declared. This is called the initialization of the variable.<br>In C++, there are three ways to initialize variables:<br>The first one, known as c-like initialization:<br>A second method, known as constructor initialization (introduced by the C++ language):<br>Finally, a third method, known as uniform initialization:<br>36<br>24/03/2025<br>type identifier = initial_value;<br>type identifier (initial_value);<br>type identifier {initial_value};</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/037.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 37: Variables (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 37/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables (cont.)<br>Example: Initialization of variables<br>37<br>24/03/2025<br>Output:</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/038.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 38: Variables (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 38/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables (cont.)<br>Type Inference in C++: auto and decltype<br>When a new variable is initialized, the compiler can figure out what the type of the variable is automatically by the initializer.<br>Example:<br>Variables that are not initialized can also make use of type deduction with the decltype specifier:<br>Example:<br>38<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/039.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 39: Variables (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 39/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Variables (cont.)<br>Using cin for user input<br>39<br>24/03/2025<br>Output:</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/040.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 40: Constants\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 40/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Constants<br>Constants are expressions with a fixed value.<br>Using const keyword:<br>40<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/041.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 41: Constants (cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 41/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Constants (cont.)<br>Preprocessor definitions (#define)<br>41<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/042.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 42: Hands-on exercises - Slot 1\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 42/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Hands-on exercises - Slot 1</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PCP291/flm1/d02/043.webp\" alt=\"PCP291 · Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 43: Summary\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slot 01 - Introduction to C++ and Basic Syntax · slide 43/43</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Summary<br>Gained a solid understanding of C++ fundamentals and its practical applications.<br>Successfully set up and configured Dev-C++ on Windows for C++ development.<br>Learned the basic structure of a C++ program and understood its compilation process.<br>Explored C++ data types, variables, and constants in depth, enhancing knowledge of memory usage and data handling.<br>43<br>24/03/2025</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
